From: WOZIWRT <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: find a station that has been answered but not yet acked

An MLD station could associate, report every link up, and never move a byte.
The AP had no 4-address peer interface for it, the station had no idea, and
nothing ever retried. Measured twice on hardware 2026-07-29: once on a cold
boot where two agents associated at the same moment, and once - reproducibly -
by removing and re-adding a link with SETUP_LINK_RECONFIG.

The 4-address peer is created either from handle_assoc_cb(), or lazily from
ieee802_11_rx_from_unknown() when the first 4-address frame arrives. That
second path exists precisely because the frame can arrive before the
association is complete, and it is careful about it: a station that is only
WLAN_STA_ASSOC_REQ_OK gets pending_wds_enable set instead of an immediate
enable, and further down, a Class 3 frame from such a station is explicitly
ignored rather than answered with a deauth.

None of that care is reached for an MLD station, because ap_get_sta() never
returns one in that window. Its MLD fallback requires WLAN_STA_ASSOC, which is
set later, in handle_assoc_cb(), after the Assoc Response TX status. So
ieee802_11_rx_from_unknown() sees a NULL station, falls through, and sends a
deauth - which the station discards, because it is unprotected and PMF is on.

The station therefore stays associated while the AP never enables WDS for it.
And it never gets a second chance: mac80211 reports an unexpected 4-address
frame exactly once per station (WLAN_STA_4ADDR_EVENT is set and never
cleared), so every later frame is dropped in silence.

Note the asymmetry this fixes. The primary lookup a few lines above returns a
station from the hash regardless of its flags; only the MLD fallback insists on
WLAN_STA_ASSOC. Accepting WLAN_STA_ASSOC_REQ_OK as well covers exactly the
window the callers already know how to handle, and nothing more.

Signed-off-by: WOZIWRT <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/ap/sta_info.c
+++ b/src/ap/sta_info.c
@@ -85,7 +85,8 @@ struct sta_info * ap_get_sta(struct hosta
 			for (s = h->sta_list; s; s = s->next)
 				if ((!os_memcmp(s->setup_link_addr, sta, 6) ||
 				     !os_memcmp(s->addr, sta, 6)) &&
-				     s->flags & WLAN_STA_ASSOC &&
+				     s->flags & (WLAN_STA_ASSOC |
+						 WLAN_STA_ASSOC_REQ_OK) &&
 				     s->mld_info.mld_sta)
 					return s;
 		}
